<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-13170] Java thin client: Transactions functionality withLabel is broken</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-13170</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Reproducer&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
@Test
&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;public&lt;/span&gt; void testTransactions1() &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;throws&lt;/span&gt; Exception {
    &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;try&lt;/span&gt; (Ignite ignite = Ignition.start(Config.getServerConfiguration());
         IgniteClient client = Ignition.startClient(getClientConfiguration()))
    {
        ClientCache&amp;lt;&lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;Integer&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;String&lt;/span&gt;&amp;gt; cache = client.createCache(&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; ClientCacheConfiguration()
                .setName(&lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;cache&quot;&lt;/span&gt;)
                .setAtomicityMode(CacheAtomicityMode.TRANSACTIONAL));

        cache.put(1, &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;value1&quot;&lt;/span&gt;);

        &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;try&lt;/span&gt; (ClientTransaction tx = client.transactions().withLabel(&lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;asdasda&quot;&lt;/span&gt;).txStart()) {
            cache.put(1, &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;value2&quot;&lt;/span&gt;);
        }

        assertEquals(&lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;value1&quot;&lt;/span&gt;, cache.get(1));
    }
}
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Root cause: a new instance of transactions facade is created when &lt;tt&gt;withLabel&lt;/tt&gt;&#160;modificator is used. Transactions are registered in &lt;tt&gt;threadLocTxUid&lt;/tt&gt; map of this instance, but when any cache operation is performed transaction is looked only at root &lt;tt&gt;threadLocTxUid&lt;/tt&gt;&#160;map.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
